i>\n        \n        \n          <li>\n            <button class=\"download-transcript-submenu-btn\" aria-haspopup=\"true\">\n              Download transcript<i class=\"material-icons\" aria-hidden=\"true\">chevron_right</i>\n            </button>\n          </li>\n        \n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    \n    \n    <div class=\"download-menu-submenu\">\n      <ul>\n        <li>\n          <button class=\"download-submenu-back-btn\">\n            <i class=\"material-icons\" aria-hidden=\"true\">chevron_left</i> Back\n          </button>\n        </li>\n        \n        <li>\n          <a href=\"../../static_resources/18642-lecture-18-version-5_transcript.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" lang=\"en\" aria-label=\"Download transcript: English\" download>English</a>\n        </li>\n        \n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    \n  </div>\n  \n</div>\n\n<div class=\"video-tab container collapse pr-0 \" role=\"tabpanel\">\n  <div class=\"video-tab-content-section\">\n    \n  </div>\n</div>\n\n  \n</div>\n\n<p><strong>Video description:</strong> The lecture by Professor Andrew W. Lo highlights how innovative financial engineering can address major societal challenges like rare diseases and energy transition by creating diversified investment portfolios that reduce risk and attract capital. Using examples from gene therapy breakthroughs and fusion energy development, he emphasizes the critical role of new financing models in turning high-risk, long-term scientific projects into viable ventures that can generate significant social and economic returns.</p>\n",
